; ABI layout manifest self-consistency checks (wave W1, FV obligation #7).
;
; Hand-maintained mirror of docs/verification/ABI_LAYOUT_MANIFEST.tsv: every
; constant below restates one manifest cell under a mechanical name, and
; tests/abi_layout_correspondence.rs checks this mirror against the TSV cell
; by cell (and, on the running target, against the live compiler layout).
; The compiler side is pinned by vinary-tree-interop/tests/layout_contract.rs
; and vinary-tree-interop/tests/discriminant_pins.rs; this file proves the
; manifest those pins feed is structurally sound on both published tiers.
;
; Naming: o64_/s64_/a64_ and o32_/s32_/a32_ are per-field offset, size, and
; natural alignment (capped at the tier's maximum fundamental alignment, 8)
; on the LP64 and 32-bit ARM EABI (AAPCS) tiers; sz*/al* are struct totals;
; d_ enum discriminants; f_ flag bits; c_ published constants; id_ interface
; identifier bytes. AAPCS alignment facts used for a32_*: pointers, usize,
; and fn pointers align to 4; u64/f64 align to 8; u8 and u8 arrays align to 1.
;
; Every check is expected to be UNSAT in both Z3 and cvc5.
(set-logic QF_LIA)

